INFO 09-15 16:07:46 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-8bf199363bfb4451ade12a0df150f55b-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nSuch civil war is in my love and hate\nTo thee I send this written embassage,\nFor through the painter must you see his skill,\nAnd perspective it is the painter's art.\nAnd do whate'er thou wilt, swift-footed Time,\nHow can I then return in happy plight,\nBut that thou none lovest is most evident;\nSuns of the world may stain when heaven's sun staineth.\nAnd that fresh blood which youngly thou bestowest\nTo that sweet thief which sourly robs from me.\nAnd loathsome canker lives in sweetest bud.\nBut if thou live, remember'd not to be,\nSo should my papers yellow'd with their age\nHow far I toil, still farther off from thee.\nSo should my papers yellow'd with their age\nFor beauty's pattern to succeeding men.\nWhich I new pay as if not paid before.\nThe dear repose for limbs with travel tired;\nWhich though it alter not love's sole effect,\nLifts up his burning head, each under eye\nClouds and eclipses stain both moon and sun,\nAll men make faults, and even I in this,\nWhich in my bosom's shop is hanging still,\nSuch civil war is in my love and hate\nFor thou art so possess'd with murderous hate\nEven so my sun one early morn did shine\nYet in these thoughts myself almost despising,\nO'ercharged with burden of mine own love's might.\nThen, beauteous niggard, why dost thou abuse<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 28576, 8202, 3653, 563, 528, 1041, 2765, 532, 17554, 107, 2021, 44543, 564, 5039, 672, 5267, 6286, 702, 676, 236764, 107, 2542, 1343, 506, 42289, 1921, 611, 1460, 914, 12889, 236764, 107, 3133, 11521, 625, 563, 506, 42289, 236789, 236751, 1610, 236761, 107, 3133, 776, 