INFO 09-15 16:07:46 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-1e51e71bbe84430f82581c583473bb47-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nAnd puts apparel on my tatter'd loving,\nThe offender's sorrow lends but weak relief\nOr any of these all, or all, or more,\nHow far I toil, still farther off from thee.\nWhen lofty trees I see barren of leaves\nEven so my sun one early morn did shine\nThat I in thy abundance am sufficed\nAnd barren rage of death's eternal cold?\nAlthough our undivided loves are one:\nYet, do thy worst, old Time: despite thy wrong,\nLest my bewailed guilt should do thee shame,\nAnd by a part of all thy glory live.\nWhich I by lacking have supposed dead,\nDuty so great, which wit so poor as mine\nIf ten of thine ten times refigured thee:\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nAs an unperfect actor on the stage\nWeary with toil, I haste me to my bed,\nFor to thy sensual fault I bring in sense--\nHast thou, the master-mistress of my passion;\nAnd puts apparel on my tatter'd loving,\nThey draw but what they see, know not the heart.\nMark how one string, sweet husband to another,\nDelights to peep, to gaze therein on thee;\nFor whether beauty, birth, or wealth, or wit,\nThe lovely gaze where every eye doth dwell,\nBut that I hope some good conceit of thine\nWho plead for love and look for recompense\nOr else of thee this I prognosticate:<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 3133, 15360, 53981, 580, 1041, 494, 2737, 236789, 236753, 22274, 236764, 107, 818, 61206, 236789, 236751, 55180, 89091, 840, 7209, 11277, 107, 3524, 1027, 529, 1239, 784, 236764, 653, 784, 236764, 653, 919, 236764, 107, 3910, 2793, 564, 141001, 236764, 2036, 41691, 1135, 699, 44543, 236761, 107, 4420, 102080, 7146, 564, 1460, 