INFO 09-15 16:07:57 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-bf5baef6b1fc45688f1a4f1ce5066686-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nFor shame! deny that thou bear'st love to any,\nSo thou, thyself out-going in thy noon,\nThough in our lives a separable spite,\nTo the wide world and all her fading sweets;\nThose hours, that with gentle work did frame\nThat this huge stage presenteth nought but shows\nCheered and cheque'd even by the self-same sky,\nA woman's face with Nature's own hand painted\nTake all my comfort of thy worth and truth.\nTo see his active child do deeds of youth,\nI will not praise that purpose not to sell.\nO, learn to read what silent love hath writ:\nWhere I may not remove nor be removed.\nO, carve not with thy hours my love's fair brow,\nDevouring Time, blunt thou the lion's paws,\nThen of thy beauty do I question make,\nDuty so great, which wit so poor as mine\nThe bounteous largess given thee to give?\nSince sweets and beauties do themselves forsake\nSuns of the world may stain when heaven's sun staineth.\nThat thou no form of thee hast left behind,\nUnless thou take that honour from thy name:\nOr any of these all, or all, or more,\nFor all that beauty that doth cover thee\nTo say, within thine own deep-sunken eyes,\nProfitless usurer, why dost thou use\nBy unions married, do offend thine ear,\nNo longer yours than you yourself here live:\nWill play the tyrants to the very same<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 2542, 30720, 236888, 30590, 600, 35627, 10591, 236789, 540, 2765, 531, 1027, 236764, 107, 4324, 35627, 236764, 208224, 883, 855, 236772, 8946, 528, 21820, 37170, 236764, 107, 31382, 528, 1023, 6176, 496, 82155, 28719, 236764, 107, 2021, 506, 5777, 1902, 532, 784, 1116, 74354,