INFO 09-15 16:07:58 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-1d1ce5340544437786d447c2e3564295-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nWhich in my bosom's shop is hanging still,\nAnd each, though enemies to either's reign,\nWhich happies those that pay the willing loan;\nFor beauty's pattern to succeeding men.\nAnd die as fast as they see others grow;\nMakes black night beauteous and her old face new.\nNor can I fortune to brief minutes tell,\nThy bosom is endeared with all hearts,\nSweets with sweets war not, joy delights in joy.\nAnd by a part of all thy glory live.\nAn eye more bright than theirs, less false in rolling,\nWhich this, Time's pencil, or my pupil pen,\nMakes black night beauteous and her old face new.\nWhen I consider every thing that grows\nThen being ask'd where all thy beauty lies,\nIf I could write the beauty of your eyes\nHarsh featureless and rude, barrenly perish:\nAnd in themselves their pride lies buried,\nA man in hue, all 'hues' in his controlling,\nHung with the trophies of my lovers gone,\nAnd make the earth devour her own sweet brood;\nThen what could death do, if thou shouldst depart,\nThat's for thyself to breed another thee,\nBut when in thee time's furrows I behold,\nOr to thyself at least kind-hearted prove:\nWho all in one, one pleasing note do sing:\nSuch civil war is in my love and hate\nMake sweet some vial; treasure thou some place\nAh! but those tears are pearl which thy love sheds,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 24249, 528, 1041, 147851, 236789, 236751, 7805, 563, 17940, 2036, 236764, 107, 3133, 1546, 236764, 3635, 22816, 531, 3477, 236789, 236751, 28797, 236764, 107, 24249, 2239, 695, 1724, 600, 2350, 506, 10788, 10670, 236793, 107, 2542, 9899, 236789, 236751, 37