INFO 09-15 16:07:58 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-19317855ff344327b7377711ead44cc6-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nAnd trouble deal heaven with my bootless cries\nThe offender's sorrow lends but weak relief\nIf I could write the beauty of your eyes\nMay make seem bare, in wanting words to show it,\nAnd yet methinks I have astronomy,\nAnd though they be outstripp'd by every pen,\nAnd fortify yourself in your decay\nO, therefore, love, be of thyself so wary\nEntitled in thy parts do crowned sit,\nO' let me, true in love, but truly write,\nAnd your true rights be term'd a poet's rage\nSo great a sum of sums, yet canst not live?\nAlthough our undivided loves are one:\nGilding the object whereupon it gazeth;\nTill then not show my head where thou mayst prove me.\nUnlook'd for joy in that I honour most.\nBut beauty's waste hath in the world an end,\nNow see what good turns eyes for eyes have done:\nFor having traffic with thyself alone,\nNow is the time that face should form another;\nWhen that churl Death my bones with dust shall cover,\nWhose strength's abundance weakens his own heart.\nWhen I behold the violet past prime,\nA man in hue, all 'hues' in his controlling,\nO' let me, true in love, but truly write,\nThy merit hath my duty strongly knit,\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat use is not forbidden usury,\nProfitless usurer, why dost thou use<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 3133, 13007, 3772, 20808, 607, 1041, 15451, 1933, 73545, 107, 818, 61206, 236789, 236751, 55180, 89091, 840, 7209, 11277, 107, 2859, 564, 1451, 4903, 506, 9899, 529, 822, 6114, 107, 12055, 1386, 4483, 13759, 236764, 528, 23021, 4171, 531, 1407, 625, 236764, 107, 3133, 3819, 17914, 24255, 564, 735, 805