INFO 09-15 16:07:58 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-9df30a2aba16492da92f226e7cdc9f8b-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nIf from thyself to store thou wouldst convert;\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nThat use is not forbidden usury,\nDo in consent shake hands to torture me;\nTill whatsoever star that guides my moving\nOf public honour and proud titles boast,\nThen let not winter's ragged hand deface\nFor never-resting time leads summer on\nAnd make the earth devour her own sweet brood;\nSo long as men can breathe or eyes can see,\nA liquid prisoner pent in walls of glass,\nNor thou with public kindness honour me,\nAnd all those friends which I thought buried.\nGilding pale streams with heavenly alchemy;\nResembling strong youth in his middle age,\nGreat princes' favourites their fair leaves spread\nWhich I by lacking have supposed dead,\nSave breed, to brave him when he takes thee hence.\nEntitled in thy parts do crowned sit,\nSo great a sum of sums, yet canst not live?\nThen can I drown an eye, unused to flow,\nThat use is not forbidden usury,\nFor thou art so possess'd with murderous hate\nMusic to hear, why hear'st thou music sadly?\nAnd that unfair which fairly doth excel:\nAnd all the rest forgot for which he toil'd:\nThat on himself such murderous shame commits.\nThen can I grieve at grievances foregone,\nDesiring this man's art and that man's scope,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 2859, 699, 208224, 883, 531, 4762, 35627, 1093, 540, 7352, 236793, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 6372, 1161, 563, 711, 47521, 775, 2623, 236764, 107, 6294, 528, 13782, 31716, 4916, 531, 55313, 786, 236793, 107, 112222, 45436, 4381, 600, 26309, 10