INFO 09-15 16:08:42 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-e443dbfa5b6147489b1ec370d55d9c87-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nWhose speechless song, being many, seeming one,\nOr else receivest with pleasure thine annoy?\nAnd burn the long-lived phoenix in her blood;\nSeeking that beauteous roof to ruinate\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nI sigh the lack of many a thing I sought,\nOr to thyself at least kind-hearted prove:\nAnd sable curls all silver'd o'er with white;\nEntitled in thy parts do crowned sit,\nMake sweet some vial; treasure thou some place\nO, that you were yourself! but, love, you are\nAs any mother's child, though not so bright\nTheirs for their style I'll read, his for his love.'\nWhich, used, lives th' executor to be.\nYourself again after yourself's decease,\nWho plead for love and look for recompense\nThe sad account of fore-bemoaned moan,\nAfter a thousand victories once foil'd,\nShe carved thee for her seal, and meant thereby\nTo say, within thine own deep-sunken eyes,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nAnd shalt by fortune once more re-survey\nWhich erst from heat did canopy the herd,\nAnd in themselves their pride lies buried,\nNeither in inward worth nor outward fair,\nMuch liker than your painted counterfeit:\nThey draw but what they see, know not the heart.\nO, let my books be then the eloquence<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 2825, 888, 160132, 5410, 236764, 1646, 1551, 236764, 109785, 886, 236764, 107, 3524, 1663, 2252, 648, 598, 607, 17132, 162531, 26259, 236881, 107, 3133, 8141, 506, 1440, 236772, 51505, 133099, 528, 1116, 4806, 23