 30%|██▉       | 295/1000 [01:07<01:02, 11.34it/s]INFO 09-15 16:08:54 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-20c5155ec3994dbeac876f850dd98745-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nO, therefore, love, be of thyself so wary\nDesiring this man's art and that man's scope,\nProfitless usurer, why dost thou use\nWhere I may not remove nor be removed.\nLet them say more than like of hearsay well;\nWhich in thy breast doth live, as thine in me:\nAgainst this coming end you should prepare,\nOr else of thee this I prognosticate:\nAnd they are rich and ransom all ill deeds.\nMy glass shall not persuade me I am old,\nWhen I behold the violet past prime,\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nThen, were not summer's distillation left,\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nOr to thyself at least kind-hearted prove:\nWith April's first-born flowers, and all things rare\nAnd nothing 'gainst Time's scythe can make defence\nLet them say more than like of hearsay well;\nMine be thy love and thy love's use their treasure.\nNo love toward others in that bosom sits\nTo work my mind, when body's work's expired:\nAnd summer's lease hath all too short a date:\nAnd often is his gold complexion dimm'd;\nPluck the keen teeth from the fierce tiger's jaws,\nI make my love engrafted to this store:\nAs interest of the dead, which now appear\nWho for thyself art so unprovident.\nWhich husbandry in honour might uphold\nThe world will be thy widow and still weep<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 236806, 236764, 5233, 236764, 2765, 236764, 577, 529, 208224, 883, 834, 79772, 107, 3984, 5935, 672, 880, 236789, 236751, 1610, 532, 600, 880, 236789, 236751, 11104, 236764, 107, 109048, 1933, 775, 7355, 236764, 3217, 24873, 35627, 1161, 107, 10