INFO 09-15 16:09:13 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-8ecefd68a9c44446ab6b9cb17e99e915-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nSo I, for fear of trust, forget to say\nSo flatter I the swart-complexion'd night,\nSo great a sum of sums, yet canst not live?\nFor never-resting time leads summer on\nThy adverse party is thy advocate--\nBut not to tell of good or evil luck,\nIn thee thy summer, ere thou be distill'd:\nThou mayst call thine when thou from youth convertest.\nThat 'gainst thyself thou stick'st not to conspire.\nAnd perspective it is the painter's art.\nExceeded by the height of happier men.\nWhen I consider every thing that grows\nThat I in thy abundance am sufficed\nRough winds do shake the darling buds of May,\nIf ten of thine ten times refigured thee:\nyet mortal looks adore his beauty still,\nBut I forbid thee one most heinous crime:\nO, carve not with thy hours my love's fair brow,\nWhich this, Time's pencil, or my pupil pen,\nOr else receivest with pleasure thine annoy?\nAnd being frank she lends to those are free.\nO, therefore, love, be of thyself so wary\nIn thee thy summer, ere thou be distill'd:\nHim in thy course untainted do allow\nAll losses are restored and sorrows end.\nThe bounteous largess given thee to give?\nWhy didst thou promise such a beauteous day,\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nBorne on the bier with white and bristly beard,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 4324, 564, 236764, 573, 9891, 529, 5210, 236764, 10849, 531, 1879, 107, 4324, 111771, 564, 506, 2353, 661, 236772, 34622, 526, 236789, 236753, 3446, 236764, 107, 4324, 1822, 496, 2324, 529, 31945, 236764, 3819, 740, 540, 711, 3892, 236881, 107, 2542, 2752, 236772, 197012, 990, 9025, 5312, 580, 107, 195