INFO 09-15 16:09:13 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-3d58f2b7d00945229cf37627f2f933ff-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nUnless thou take that honour from thy name:\nBeauty o'ersnow'd and bareness every where:\nNo more be grieved at that which thou hast done:\nIn thy soul's thought, all naked, will bestow it;\nSap cheque'd with frost and lusty leaves quite gone,\nSo I, made lame by fortune's dearest spite,\nWill play the tyrants to the very same\nThy unused beauty must be tomb'd with thee,\nThen happy I, that love and am beloved\nThat on himself such murderous shame commits.\nThe lovely gaze where every eye doth dwell,\nAuthorizing thy trespass with compare,\nWith all triumphant splendor on my brow;\nMusic to hear, why hear'st thou music sadly?\nBorne on the bier with white and bristly beard,\nO, learn to read what silent love hath writ:\nLet them say more than like of hearsay well;\nKissing with golden face the meadows green,\nIs but the seemly raiment of my heart,\nMore than that tongue that more hath more express'd.\nAnd loathsome canker lives in sweetest bud.\nSo thou, thyself out-going in thy noon,\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd your sweet semblance to some other give.\nAnd loathsome canker lives in sweetest bud.\nAfter a thousand victories once foil'd,\nThou art more lovely and more temperate:\nOr who is he so fond will be the tomb\nBut were some child of yours alive that time,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 71520, 35627, 1769, 600, 20488, 699, 21820, 1463, 236787, 107, 74722, 512, 236789, 616, 2998, 236789, 236753, 532, 13759, 1788, 1418, 1298, 236787, 107, 3771, 919, 577, 66031, 1872, 657, 600, 837, 35627, 23823, 3028, 236787, 107, 902, 21820, 12556, 236789, 23675