 38%|███▊      | 377/1000 [01:28<01:33,  6.64it/s]INFO 09-15 16:09:14 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-613d0eb1cf784f75a001c2d3e96353d0-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nAnd loathsome canker lives in sweetest bud.\nThen may I dare to boast how I do love thee;\nWhen, in disgrace with fortune and men's eyes,\nYou should live twice; in it and in my rhyme.\nThese poor rude lines of thy deceased lover,\nThen can I grieve at grievances foregone,\nStealing unseen to west with this disgrace:\nTo thee I send this written embassage,\nFor where is she so fair whose unear'd womb\nBut when in thee time's furrows I behold,\nSo should that beauty which you hold in lease\nResembling sire and child and happy mother\nFor never-resting time leads summer on\nAnd dost him grace when clouds do blot the heaven:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nAnd burn the long-lived phoenix in her blood;\nCalls back the lovely April of her prime:\nCan make you live yourself in eyes of men.\nWithout thy help by me be borne alone.\nO, learn to read what silent love hath writ:\nA woman's face with Nature's own hand painted\nResembling strong youth in his middle age,\nBut not to tell of good or evil luck,\nFor no man well of such a salve can speak\nBut out, alack! he was but one hour mine;\nMay make seem bare, in wanting words to show it,\nWhich husbandry in honour might uphold\nWhy didst thou promise such a beauteous day,\nThe region cloud hath mask'd him from me now.<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 3133, 1510, 651, 19256, 740, 5806, 6176, 528, 155753, 5207, 236761, 107, 11407, 1149, 564, 30253, 531, 70447, 1217, 564, 776, 2765, 44543, 236793, 107, 4420, 236764, 528, 87270, 607, 31252, 532, 1758, 236789, 236751, 6114, 23