 40%|████      | 400/1000 [01:28<00:35, 16.85it/s]INFO 09-15 16:09:15 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-a4ff556b20334a0f8f759f3ce5c21e37-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nNor draw no lines there with thine antique pen;\nThou shouldst print more, not let that copy die.\nWhich, like a jewel hung in ghastly night,\nIf it were fill'd with your most high deserts?\nWho with his fear is put besides his part,\nO, learn to read what silent love hath writ:\nYou should live twice; in it and in my rhyme.\nClouds and eclipses stain both moon and sun,\nThen being ask'd where all thy beauty lies,\nBeauty o'ersnow'd and bareness every where:\nBut that I hope some good conceit of thine\nPointing to each his thunder, rain and wind,\nThou mayst call thine when thou from youth convertest.\nWhich in my bosom's shop is hanging still,\nSave breed, to brave him when he takes thee hence.\nRough winds do shake the darling buds of May,\nIf ten of thine ten times refigured thee:\nBut do not so; I love thee in such sort\nBy unions married, do offend thine ear,\nSo is it not with me as with that Muse\nThou art more lovely and more temperate:\nThat then I scorn to change my state with kings.\nBut that thou none lovest is most evident;\nBut since she prick'd thee out for women's pleasure,\nAnd you must live, drawn by your own sweet skill.\nThe world will be thy widow and still weep\nBut were some child of yours alive that time,\nAnd kept unused, the user so destroys it.\nYourself again after yourself's decease,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 31777, 4988, 951, 4463, 993, 607, 162531, 34323, 4306, 236793, 107, 178651, 1374, 540, 1887, 919, 236764, 711, 1531, 600, 4865, 1778, 236761, 107, 24249, 236764, 1133, 496, 71102, 1541