 42%|████▏     | 416/1000 [01:38<02:45,  3.54it/s]INFO 09-15 16:09:24 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-d21d26323bd548a6b4888dd60fc4e79b-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nBy chance or nature's changing course untrimm'd;\nAnd see thy blood warm when thou feel'st it cold.\nTo change your day of youth to sullied night;\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nAnd see thy blood warm when thou feel'st it cold.\nProfitless usurer, why dost thou use\nLet those whom Nature hath not made for store,\nProving his beauty by succession thine!\nSince sweets and beauties do themselves forsake\n'Had my friend's Muse grown with this growing age,\nAnd 'gainst myself a lawful plea commence:\nLook in thy glass, and tell the face thou viewest\nAnd keep my drooping eyelids open wide,\nNo love toward others in that bosom sits\nCheered and cheque'd even by the self-same sky,\nClouds and eclipses stain both moon and sun,\nNor can I fortune to brief minutes tell,\nWith sun and moon, with earth and sea's rich gems,\nIn thy soul's thought, all naked, will bestow it;\nFrom sullen earth, sings hymns at heaven's gate;\nTill Nature, as she wrought thee, fell a-doting,\nAnd see thy blood warm when thou feel'st it cold.\nThat beauty still may live in thine or thee.\nIs from the book of honour razed quite,\nAnd yet methinks I have astronomy,\nA man in hue, all 'hues' in his controlling,\nThe dear repose for limbs with travel tired;\nBut were some child of yours alive that time,\nShifts but his place, for still the world enjoys it;<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 2292, 6584, 653, 4135, 236789, 236751, 9199, 3003, 2225, 4966, 236757, 236789, 236753, 236793, 107, 3133, 1460, 21820, 4806, 6962, 1056, 35627, 2597, 236789, 54