 42%|████▏     | 421/1000 [01:38<02:02,  4.74it/s]INFO 09-15 16:09:24 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-7ed1f1a2729942bf885cdaaab5d5bfeb-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nAnd do whate'er thou wilt, swift-footed Time,\nLooking on darkness which the blind do see\nBut things removed that hidden in thee lie!\nAnd all in war with Time for love of you,\nDelights to peep, to gaze therein on thee;\nThe bounteous largess given thee to give?\nProving his beauty by succession thine!\nThe perfect ceremony of love's rite,\nTake all my comfort of thy worth and truth.\nSuch civil war is in my love and hate\nYet doth it steal sweet hours from love's delight.\nHow can I then be elder than thou art?\nSo should my papers yellow'd with their age\nLooking on darkness which the blind do see\nWho plead for love and look for recompense\nTheirs for their style I'll read, his for his love.'\nThough thou repent, yet I have still the loss:\nIs from the book of honour razed quite,\nWhich erst from heat did canopy the herd,\nAnd do whate'er thou wilt, swift-footed Time,\nAnd each, though enemies to either's reign,\nLo! thus, by day my limbs, by night my mind,\nUnthrifty loveliness, why dost thou spend\nIf thou couldst answer 'This fair child of mine\nWho all in one, one pleasing note do sing:\nOr else receivest with pleasure thine annoy?\nMuch liker than your painted counterfeit:\nProving his beauty by succession thine!\nIn thy soul's thought, all naked, will bestow it;<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 3133, 776, 615, 606, 236789, 497, 35627, 71438, 236764, 37884, 236772, 143766, 7578, 236764, 107, 30988, 580, 29151, 837, 506, 18261, 776, 1460, 107, 4573, 2432, 8476, 600, 11497, 528, 44543, 7089, 236888, 107, 3133, 784, 52