 44%|████▍     | 444/1000 [01:39<00:40, 13.83it/s]INFO 09-15 16:09:25 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-bae585d305e848b4bf8b0f38896fdade-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nAgainst the stormy gusts of winter's day\nAnd by a part of all thy glory live.\nFor beauty's pattern to succeeding men.\nLook, what an unthrift in the world doth spend\nAnd for a woman wert thou first created;\nThen can I grieve at grievances foregone,\nAnd from the forlorn world his visage hide,\nAnd all those friends which I thought buried.\nWhich husbandry in honour might uphold\nThen what could death do, if thou shouldst depart,\nAnd keep my drooping eyelids open wide,\nBut day by night, and night by day, oppress'd?\nAs an unperfect actor on the stage\nAfter a thousand victories once foil'd,\nThy beauty's form in table of my heart;\nTo the wide world and all her fading sweets;\nBe not self-will'd, for thou art much too fair\nSo I, made lame by fortune's dearest spite,\nAnd nothing 'gainst Time's scythe can make defence\nMark how one string, sweet husband to another,\nWhere I may not remove nor be removed.\nThou art thy mother's glass, and she in thee\nUnthrifty loveliness, why dost thou spend\nSo should that beauty which you hold in lease\nIn our two loves there is but one respect,\nWhen I perceive that men as plants increase,\nNo love toward others in that bosom sits\nBut that thou none lovest is most evident;\nIf it were fill'd with your most high deserts?<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 91561, 506, 89373, 186031, 529, 7208, 236789, 236751, 1719, 107, 3133, 684, 496, 912, 529, 784, 21820, 27877, 3892, 236761, 107, 2542, 9899, 236789, 236751, 3759, 531, 60207, 1758, 236761, 107, 13908, 236764, 1144, 614, 723, 200090, 52