 45%|████▌     | 454/1000 [01:48<05:07,  1.78it/s]INFO 09-15 16:09:34 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-198959709b9a4f03bc95c89945ed55a0-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nSo long lives this and this gives life to thee.\nWhen to the sessions of sweet silent thought\nBut beauty's waste hath in the world an end,\nHiding thy bravery in their rotten smoke?\nYet, do thy worst, old Time: despite thy wrong,\nAnd having climb'd the steep-up heavenly hill,\nStrikes each in each by mutual ordering,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nAfter a thousand victories once foil'd,\nThat due of many now is thine alone:\nThou dost beguile the world, unbless some mother.\nBut out, alack! he was but one hour mine;\nLike to the lark at break of day arising\nHow far I toil, still farther off from thee.\nMusic to hear, why hear'st thou music sadly?\nHow can I then return in happy plight,\nAnd, constant stars, in them I read such art\nAnd summer's green all girded up in sheaves\nWhy didst thou promise such a beauteous day,\nThat due of many now is thine alone:\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nTo dry the rain on my storm-beaten face,\nMy love shall in my verse ever live young.\nBy children's eyes her husband's shape in mind.\nTo change your day of youth to sullied night;\nI summon up remembrance of things past,\nThe region cloud hath mask'd him from me now.\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nWhich in thy breast doth live, as thine in me:<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 4324, 1440, 6176, 672, 532, 672, 5021, 1972, 531, 44543, 236761, 107, 4420, 531, 506, 14845, 529, 9380, 24782, 3305, 107, 4573, 9899, 236789, 236751, 8321, 46440, 528, 506, 1902, 614, 1345, 236764, 107, 236814, 3651, 21820, 101666, 5