INFO 09-15 16:09:35 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-60cee629b18e420c96aa93c51dc76adf-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nSo flatter I the swart-complexion'd night,\nBut if the while I think on thee, dear friend,\nAnd make me travel forth without my cloak,\nDuty so great, which wit so poor as mine\nThen how, when nature calls thee to be gone,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nSometime too hot the eye of heaven shines,\nThat then I scorn to change my state with kings.\nTo be death's conquest and make worms thine heir.\nBeauty o'ersnow'd and bareness every where:\nMyself corrupting, salving thy amiss,\nDo in consent shake hands to torture me;\nNeither in inward worth nor outward fair,\nAnd in fresh numbers number all your graces,\nFor no man well of such a salve can speak\nHow far I toil, still farther off from thee.\nThy youth's proud livery, so gazed on now,\nAs those gold candles fix'd in heaven's air:\nAnd in mine own love's strength seem to decay,\nAnd sable curls all silver'd o'er with white;\nThen may I dare to boast how I do love thee;\nFor all that beauty that doth cover thee\nLet them say more than like of hearsay well;\nTo thee I send this written embassage,\nWhen I perceive that men as plants increase,\nWhen lofty trees I see barren of leaves\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nSave that my soul's imaginary sight\nA dearer birth than this his love had brought,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 4324, 111771, 564, 506, 2353, 661, 236772, 34622, 526, 236789, 236753, 3446, 236764, 107, 4573, 768, 506, 1651, 564, 1751, 580, 44543, 236764, 23348, 4389, 236764, 107, 3133, 1386, 786, 4301, 12034, 2180, 1041, 72527, 236764, 107, 116195, 834, 1822, 236764, 837, 32950, 83