 51%|█████     | 512/1000 [01:58<02:46,  2.94it/s]INFO 09-15 16:09:45 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-0233ffcbdc2644819a8a49da8d02c1ee-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nWhich in my bosom's shop is hanging still,\nBut from thine eyes my knowledge I derive,\nO, change thy thought, that I may change my mind!\nOr who is he so fond will be the tomb\nTake all my comfort of thy worth and truth.\nAre windows to my breast, where-through the sun\nFor thou art so possess'd with murderous hate\nWhen I do count the clock that tells the time,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nI summon up remembrance of things past,\nWhen I consider every thing that grows\nLeaving thee living in posterity?\nYet him for this my love no whit disdaineth;\nThey do but sweetly chide thee, who confounds\nThe lovely gaze where every eye doth dwell,\nFor thy sweet love remember'd such wealth brings\nWishing me like to one more rich in hope,\nTo say, within thine own deep-sunken eyes,\nMusic to hear, why hear'st thou music sadly?\nThe dear repose for limbs with travel tired;\nThy unused beauty must be tomb'd with thee,\nThat am debarr'd the benefit of rest?\nFor at a frown they in their glory die.\nAnd your sweet semblance to some other give.\nBut since he died and poets better prove,\nAnd they are rich and ransom all ill deeds.\nSo great a sum of sums, yet canst not live?\nTheir images I loved I view in thee,\nProving his beauty by succession thine!<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 24249, 528, 1041, 147851, 236789, 236751, 7805, 563, 17940, 2036, 236764, 107, 4573, 699, 162531, 6114, 1041, 4654, 564, 27119, 236764, 107, 236806, 236764, 2352, 21820, 3305, 236764, 600, 564, 1149, 2352, 1041, 3666, 236888, 107, 3524, 1015, 5