 58%|█████▊    | 582/1000 [02:10<00:38, 10.73it/s]INFO 09-15 16:09:56 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-a1888e9911de43aba56cf63265ffe881-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nDelights to peep, to gaze therein on thee;\nWhich happies those that pay the willing loan;\nThe offender's sorrow lends but weak relief\nWhen I perceive that men as plants increase,\nUnthrifty loveliness, why dost thou spend\nAs, thou being mine, mine is thy good report.\nGilding the object whereupon it gazeth;\nAnd by addition me of thee defeated,\nAs truth and beauty shall together thrive,\nFor then my thoughts, from far where I abide,\nLike to the lark at break of day arising\nLest my bewailed guilt should do thee shame,\nGreat princes' favourites their fair leaves spread\nIf the true concord of well-tuned sounds,\nAgainst the stormy gusts of winter's day\nBe not self-will'd, for thou art much too fair\nBut if the while I think on thee, dear friend,\nAre windows to my breast, where-through the sun\nMine eye hath play'd the painter and hath stell'd\nThy bosom is endeared with all hearts,\nAs any mother's child, though not so bright\nOf his self-love, to stop posterity?\nIf it were fill'd with your most high deserts?\nWith sun and moon, with earth and sea's rich gems,\nLook, what an unthrift in the world doth spend\nTo change your day of youth to sullied night;\nShifts but his place, for still the world enjoys it;\nFrom sullen earth, sings hymns at heaven's gate;\nAnd that fresh blood which youngly thou bestowest<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 12846, 4821, 531, 154312, 236764, 531, 48674, 33025, 580, 44543, 236793, 107, 24249, 2239, 695, 1724, 600, 2350, 506, 10788, 10670, 236793, 107, 818, 61206, 236789, 236751, 55180, 89