 60%|██████    | 601/1000 [02:19<04:04,  1.63it/s]INFO 09-15 16:10:05 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-0e3b88d70ffc467c9dff829e9f05209a-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nThen may I dare to boast how I do love thee;\nTo change your day of youth to sullied night;\nThy beauty's form in table of my heart;\nThat 'gainst thyself thou stick'st not to conspire.\nThe offender's sorrow lends but weak relief\nAs, thou being mine, mine is thy good report.\nBut day doth daily draw my sorrows longer\nGilding the object whereupon it gazeth;\nWhen I do count the clock that tells the time,\nBe, as thy presence is, gracious and kind,\nNor thou with public kindness honour me,\nAuthorizing thy trespass with compare,\nPoints on me graciously with fair aspect\nTo march in ranks of better equipage:\nOf plagues, of dearths, or seasons' quality;\nHow can I then be elder than thou art?\nBut thy eternal summer shall not fade\nAnd each, though enemies to either's reign,\nLest my bewailed guilt should do thee shame,\nYet, do thy worst, old Time: despite thy wrong,\nWhose strength's abundance weakens his own heart.\nAnd moan the expense of many a vanish'd sight:\nTill Nature, as she wrought thee, fell a-doting,\nWhereon the stars in secret influence comment;\nWith what I most enjoy contented least;\nHow far I toil, still farther off from thee.\nIn thee thy summer, ere thou be distill'd:\nWith virtuous wish would bear your living flowers,\nThe one by toil, the other to complain<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 11407, 1149, 564, 30253, 531, 70447, 1217, 564, 776, 2765, 44543, 236793, 107, 2021, 2352, 822, 1719, 529, 10974, 531, 61862, 1178, 3446, 236793, 107, 195297, 9899, 236789, 236751, 1183, 528, 2633, 529, 1041, 3710, 2