INFO 09-15 16:10:05 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-ac5e5f57567d435caf19ad5b31dcdfdf-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nBut if thou live, remember'd not to be,\nMine eyes have drawn thy shape, and thine for me\nPresume not on thy heart when mine is slain;\nSince sweets and beauties do themselves forsake\nBut since he died and poets better prove,\nAnd loathsome canker lives in sweetest bud.\nAnd kept unused, the user so destroys it.\nWho heaven itself for ornament doth use\nFor no man well of such a salve can speak\nIs it for fear to wet a widow's eye\nThou of thyself thy sweet self dost deceive.\nAfter a thousand victories once foil'd,\nBut if the while I think on thee, dear friend,\nWhat acceptable audit canst thou leave?\nMay make seem bare, in wanting words to show it,\nMakes black night beauteous and her old face new.\nBy children's eyes her husband's shape in mind.\nShe carved thee for her seal, and meant thereby\nAfter a thousand victories once foil'd,\nO, that you were yourself! but, love, you are\nThy youth's proud livery, so gazed on now,\nSap cheque'd with frost and lusty leaves quite gone,\nThy unused beauty must be tomb'd with thee,\nThat then I scorn to change my state with kings.\nMaking a couplement of proud compare,\nOr else receivest with pleasure thine annoy?\nWhich bounteous gift thou shouldst in bounty cherish:\nHow can I then be elder than thou art?\nDoth homage to his new-appearing sight,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 4573, 768, 35627, 3892, 236764, 5630, 236789, 236753, 711, 531, 577, 236764, 107, 61781, 6114, 735, 9710, 21820, 6230, 236764, 532, 162531, 573, 786, 107, 18160, 2392, 711, 580, 21820, 3710, 1056, 10701, 563, 125947, 236793, 107, 10081, 60831, 532, 10777