 62%|██████▏   | 616/1000 [02:19<01:26,  4.43it/s]INFO 09-15 16:10:06 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-fc22ec2579954556af2bee28231ce3bf-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nStrikes each in each by mutual ordering,\nThen, beauteous niggard, why dost thou abuse\nWhich, like a jewel hung in ghastly night,\nBut day doth daily draw my sorrows longer\nYou should live twice; in it and in my rhyme.\nThen how, when nature calls thee to be gone,\nShifts but his place, for still the world enjoys it;\nAnd, constant stars, in them I read such art\nAnd there reigns love and all love's loving parts,\nWhen I perceive that men as plants increase,\nWhen forty winters shall beseige thy brow,\nAnd all the rest forgot for which he toil'd:\nThat's for thyself to breed another thee,\nAnd see thy blood warm when thou feel'st it cold.\nFrom sullen earth, sings hymns at heaven's gate;\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nThen can I drown an eye, unused to flow,\nThese poor rude lines of thy deceased lover,\nOf plagues, of dearths, or seasons' quality;\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nWho all in one, one pleasing note do sing:\nIf thou survive my well-contented day,\nAnd all in war with Time for love of you,\nWhen your sweet issue your sweet form should bear.\nThen how, when nature calls thee to be gone,\nThou gavest me thine, not to give back again.\nAnd kept unused, the user so destroys it.\nBut when in thee time's furrows I behold,\nWhich to repair should be thy chief desire.<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 155124, 10877, 1546, 528, 1546, 684, 21281, 24121, 236764, 107, 11407, 236764, 210820, 1328, 806, 116063, 714, 236764, 3217, 24873, 35627, 16407, 107, 24249, 236764, 1133, 496, 71102, 15410, 528