 63%|██████▎   | 632/1000 [02:20<00:33, 10.85it/s]INFO 09-15 16:10:06 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-f58d633755dd4ea1a504b14f8165067f-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nIf I could write the beauty of your eyes\nIf thou survive my well-contented day,\nWithout this, folly, age and cold decay:\nWill be a tatter'd weed, of small worth held:\nAnd stretched metre of an antique song:\nThy adverse party is thy advocate--\nThy unused beauty must be tomb'd with thee,\nBut since he died and poets better prove,\nBut I forbid thee one most heinous crime:\nYet, do thy worst, old Time: despite thy wrong,\nSo thou, thyself out-going in thy noon,\nReserve them for my love, not for their rhyme,\nYet in these thoughts myself almost despising,\nBut things removed that hidden in thee lie!\nBut when in thee time's furrows I behold,\nYet doth it steal sweet hours from love's delight.\nAfter a thousand victories once foil'd,\nThe eyes, 'fore duteous, now converted are\nAnd wear their brave state out of memory;\nA dearer birth than this his love had brought,\nThe dear repose for limbs with travel tired;\nAs an unperfect actor on the stage\nThen of thy beauty do I question make,\nBeauty's effect with beauty were bereft,\nRoses have thorns, and silver fountains mud;\nMake thee another self, for love of me,\nThat heals the wound and cures not the disgrace:\nSo should my papers yellow'd with their age\nThen may I dare to boast how I do love thee;<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 2859, 564, 1451, 4903, 506, 9899, 529, 822, 6114, 107, 2859, 35627, 19635, 1041, 1388, 236772, 3955, 524, 1719, 236764, 107, 33142, 672, 236764, 128005, 236764, 3911, 532, 7445, 17538, 236787, 107, 15600, 577, 496, 494, 2737, 236789, 236753, 411