 64%|██████▍   | 643/1000 [02:20<00:22, 16.00it/s]INFO 09-15 16:10:07 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-01b373c9420946a28aba4e3197c34a1a-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nAnd your sweet semblance to some other give.\nThough in our lives a separable spite,\nWhereon the stars in secret influence comment;\nIf thou couldst answer 'This fair child of mine\nAnd by a part of all thy glory live.\nFind no determination: then you were\nFor through the painter must you see his skill,\nThou art thy mother's glass, and she in thee\nShe carved thee for her seal, and meant thereby\nSo long as men can breathe or eyes can see,\nSo flatter I the swart-complexion'd night,\nYou had a father: let your son say so.\nKissing with golden face the meadows green,\nRoses have thorns, and silver fountains mud;\nFull many a glorious morning have I seen\nWhich in thy breast doth live, as thine in me:\nThen look I death my days should expiate.\nWhen I behold the violet past prime,\nAnd that unfair which fairly doth excel:\nWhen forty winters shall beseige thy brow,\nWhich husbandry in honour might uphold\nFor then my thoughts, from far where I abide,\nA man in hue, all 'hues' in his controlling,\nAnd every fair from fair sometime declines,\nAll men make faults, and even I in this,\nVaunt in their youthful sap, at height decrease,\nMine be thy love and thy love's use their treasure.\nThat 'gainst thyself thou stick'st not to conspire.\nCheered and cheque'd even by the self-same sky,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 3133, 822, 9380, 178837, 531, 1070, 1032, 2583, 236761, 107, 31382, 528, 1023, 6176, 496, 82155, 28719, 236764, 107, 10936, 498, 506, 8197, 528, 6789, 7630, 5739, 236793, 107, 2859, 35627, 1451, 540, 3890, 756, 209