INFO 09-15 16:10:17 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-5579a4d75655432b8ecbce668ab66ca1-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nTo hideous winter and confounds him there;\nWill play the tyrants to the very same\nIf ten of thine ten times refigured thee:\nWho lets so fair a house fall to decay,\nSo long as men can breathe or eyes can see,\nAnd having climb'd the steep-up heavenly hill,\nNow stand you on the top of happy hours,\nBut as the marigold at the sun's eye,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nLet those whom Nature hath not made for store,\nUnlook'd for joy in that I honour most.\nBy unions married, do offend thine ear,\nDie single, and thine image dies with thee.\nWith April's first-born flowers, and all things rare\nBorne on the bier with white and bristly beard,\nShall sum my count and make my old excuse,'\nSave that my soul's imaginary sight\nTill then not show my head where thou mayst prove me.\nLifts up his burning head, each under eye\nTo say, within thine own deep-sunken eyes,\nBut flowers distill'd though they with winter meet,\nTake all my comfort of thy worth and truth.\nThen can I drown an eye, unused to flow,\nHolds in perfection but a little moment,\nAgainst this coming end you should prepare,\nNow stand you on the top of happy hours,\nAnd die as fast as they see others grow;\nFrom sullen earth, sings hymns at heaven's gate;\nAs truth and beauty shall together thrive,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 2021, 148326, 7208, 532, 2127, 3575, 1515, 993, 236793, 107, 15600, 1441, 506, 50809, 1639, 531, 506, 1401, 1638, 107, 2859, 3595, 529, 162531, 3595, 2782, 544, 216357, 44543, 236787, 107, 15938, 19518, 834, 5888, 496, 3155, 3798, 531, 17538, 236764, 107, 4324, 1440, 618, 1758,