 70%|███████   | 701/1000 [02:40<03:02,  1.64it/s]INFO 09-15 16:10:26 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-a66d6f8823e4454a9552a05b98cfee95-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nWhilst I, whom fortune of such triumph bars,\nI make my love engrafted to this store:\nAnd puts apparel on my tatter'd loving,\nThat on himself such murderous shame commits.\nKissing with golden face the meadows green,\nA woman's gentle heart, but not acquainted\nThat hath his windows glazed with thine eyes.\nGreat princes' favourites their fair leaves spread\nAnon permit the basest clouds to ride\nAll men make faults, and even I in this,\nShifts but his place, for still the world enjoys it;\nWho with his fear is put besides his part,\nLet those whom Nature hath not made for store,\nThe eyes, 'fore duteous, now converted are\nAfter a thousand victories once foil'd,\nThen, were not summer's distillation left,\nThou art thy mother's glass, and she in thee\nDie single, and thine image dies with thee.\nGrant, if thou wilt, thou art beloved of many,\nMake thee another self, for love of me,\nAnd often is his gold complexion dimm'd;\nSets you most rich in youth before my sight,\nClouds and eclipses stain both moon and sun,\nWere an all-eating shame and thriftless praise.\nBut if the while I think on thee, dear friend,\nThat then I scorn to change my state with kings.\nThe sad account of fore-bemoaned moan,\nTo let base clouds o'ertake me in my way,\nAs fast as thou shalt wane, so fast thou growest<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 96553, 564, 236764, 8761, 31252, 529, 1288, 39786, 13163, 236764, 107, 236777, 1386, 1041, 2765, 2336, 183114, 531, 672, 4762, 236787, 107, 3133, 15360, 53981, 580, 1041, 494, 2737, 236789, 236753, 22274, 2