 72%|███████▏  | 716/1000 [02:41<01:03,  4.47it/s]INFO 09-15 16:10:27 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-462144faf6ef4101b035c41217f8864a-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nPresents thy shadow to my sightless view,\nShe carved thee for her seal, and meant thereby\nThat hath his windows glazed with thine eyes.\nO'ercharged with burden of mine own love's might.\nFor through the painter must you see his skill,\nCalls back the lovely April of her prime:\nEntitled in thy parts do crowned sit,\nAh! if thou issueless shalt hap to die.\nThat heaven's air in this huge rondure hems.\nTill Nature, as she wrought thee, fell a-doting,\nTheir images I loved I view in thee,\nThat use is not forbidden usury,\nProfitless usurer, why dost thou use\nDuty so great, which wit so poor as mine\nProving his beauty by succession thine!\nThat then I scorn to change my state with kings.\nSo I, for fear of trust, forget to say\nLook, what an unthrift in the world doth spend\nLet those whom Nature hath not made for store,\nIn thee thy summer, ere thou be distill'd:\nHung with the trophies of my lovers gone,\nWho with his fear is put besides his part,\nI may not evermore acknowledge thee,\nBe scorn'd like old men of less truth than tongue,\nAs an unperfect actor on the stage\nDuty so great, which wit so poor as mine\nReserve them for my love, not for their rhyme,\nAnd fortify yourself in your decay<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 236791, 8872, 21820, 13024, 531, 1041, 14186, 1933, 1927, 236764, 107, 5778, 39043, 44543, 573, 1116, 18505, 236764, 532, 9655, 17534, 107, 6372, 46440, 914, 11665, 77842, 607, 162531, 6114, 236761, 10