INFO 09-15 16:10:27 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-262916c0511643e5abcada5e5d03332c-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nDo in consent shake hands to torture me;\nBy adding one thing to my purpose nothing.\nAnd threescore year would make the world away.\nNot from the stars do I my judgment pluck;\nNow is the time that face should form another;\nDesiring this man's art and that man's scope,\nWhich I new pay as if not paid before.\nSo should that beauty which you hold in lease\nIf all were minded so, the times should cease\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nHaply I think on thee, and then my state,\nAnd that unfair which fairly doth excel:\nWhen your sweet issue your sweet form should bear.\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nA liquid prisoner pent in walls of glass,\nI will not praise that purpose not to sell.\nAll losses are restored and sorrows end.\nThey draw but what they see, know not the heart.\nMy glass shall not persuade me I am old,\nOf his self-love, to stop posterity?\nPointing to each his thunder, rain and wind,\nEntitled in thy parts do crowned sit,\nClouds and eclipses stain both moon and sun,\nAll losses are restored and sorrows end.\nEven so my sun one early morn did shine\nAnd then believe me, my love is as fair\nThy youth's proud livery, so gazed on now,\nCalls back the lovely April of her prime:\nWhen in eternal lines to time thou growest:<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 6294, 528, 13782, 31716, 4916, 531, 55313, 786, 236793, 107, 2292, 8009, 886, 3210, 531, 1041, 5708, 5017, 236761, 107, 3133, 155173, 6102, 1051, 1093, 1386, 506, 1902, 3121, 236761, 107, 4348, 699, 506, 8197, 776, 564, 1041, 11179, 179196, 236793, 107, 6445, 563, 506, 990, 600, 3392, 13