 79%|███████▊  | 786/1000 [02:52<00:16, 12.68it/s]INFO 09-15 16:10:38 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-074b29f447044903aeca9409edf77f79-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nO' let me, true in love, but truly write,\nWhich, like a jewel hung in ghastly night,\nBy oft predict that I in heaven find:\nMuch steals men's eyes and women's souls amazeth.\nMy glass shall not persuade me I am old,\nAnd there reigns love and all love's loving parts,\nYet in these thoughts myself almost despising,\nAnd stretched metre of an antique song:\nI sigh the lack of many a thing I sought,\nAnd die as fast as they see others grow;\nA liquid prisoner pent in walls of glass,\nO' let me, true in love, but truly write,\nBut since he died and poets better prove,\nAnd being frank she lends to those are free.\nDespite of wrinkles this thy golden time.\nAre windows to my breast, where-through the sun\nAs a decrepit father takes delight\nThat I an accessary needs must be\nAnd keep my drooping eyelids open wide,\nAnd you must live, drawn by your own sweet skill.\nWeary with toil, I haste me to my bed,\nBut out, alack! he was but one hour mine;\nSeeking that beauteous roof to ruinate\nPresume not on thy heart when mine is slain;\nThey do but sweetly chide thee, who confounds\nIf it were fill'd with your most high deserts?\nA woman's face with Nature's own hand painted\nUnlook'd on diest, unless thou get a son.\nDisdains the tillage of thy husbandry?<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 236806, 236789, 1531, 786, 236764, 1847, 528, 2765, 236764, 840, 9995, 4903, 236764, 107, 24249, 236764, 1133, 496, 71102, 15410, 528, 29160, 224659, 3446, 236764, 107, 2292, 39179, 4773, 600, 564, 528, 20808, 1586, 236787, 107, 46003, 88541, 1758, 2