INFO 09-15 16:10:47 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-594f05b479404b688ebf7e1f40b261d9-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nI make my love engrafted to this store:\nHow far I toil, still farther off from thee.\nNor draw no lines there with thine antique pen;\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nThen may I dare to boast how I do love thee;\nLord of my love, to whom in vassalage\nThe region cloud hath mask'd him from me now.\nTo see his active child do deeds of youth,\nAnd night doth nightly make grief's strength seem stronger.\nAs, thou being mine, mine is thy good report.\nAnd make me travel forth without my cloak,\nEven so my sun one early morn did shine\nEntitled in thy parts do crowned sit,\nWith sun and moon, with earth and sea's rich gems,\nDie single, and thine image dies with thee.\nThe offender's sorrow lends but weak relief\nWhen every private widow well may keep\nAnd in themselves their pride lies buried,\nWhere I may not remove nor be removed.\nWhy lovest thou that which thou receivest not gladly,\nWishing me like to one more rich in hope,\nStirr'd by a painted beauty to his verse,\nMaking a couplement of proud compare,\nIf thou couldst answer 'This fair child of mine\nTo march in ranks of better equipage:\nSo I, made lame by fortune's dearest spite,\nAnd dig deep trenches in thy beauty's field,\nHung with the trophies of my lovers gone,\nWho with his fear is put besides his part,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 236777, 1386, 1041, 2765, 2336, 183114, 531, 672, 4762, 236787, 107, 3910, 2793, 564, 141001, 236764, 2036, 41691, 1135, 699, 44543, 236761, 107, 31777, 4988, 951, 4463, 993, 607, 162531, 34323, 4306, 236793, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5