 83%|████████▎ | 826/1000 [03:02<00:26,  6.48it/s]INFO 09-15 16:10:48 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-b8d24ede53124ce983f7fecf93057401-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nAh! if thou issueless shalt hap to die.\nMy love shall in my verse ever live young.\nBut then begins a journey in my head,\nThen look I death my days should expiate.\nAnd dumb presagers of my speaking breast,\nSweets with sweets war not, joy delights in joy.\nO, therefore, love, be of thyself so wary\nOr who is he so fond will be the tomb\nThe painful warrior famoused for fight,\nWhich husbandry in honour might uphold\nAttending on his golden pilgrimage;\nAnd burn the long-lived phoenix in her blood;\nFor then my thoughts, from far where I abide,\nBut if thou live, remember'd not to be,\nBut day doth daily draw my sorrows longer\nSo long as youth and thou are of one date;\nThe world will wail thee, like a makeless wife;\nNow stand you on the top of happy hours,\nTo that sweet thief which sourly robs from me.\nWhen lofty trees I see barren of leaves\nAnd shalt by fortune once more re-survey\nPluck the keen teeth from the fierce tiger's jaws,\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFor beauty's pattern to succeeding men.\nDuty so great, which wit so poor as mine\nSo is it not with me as with that Muse\nYou had a father: let your son say so.\nMore than that tongue that more hath more express'd.\nSo should my papers yellow'd with their age<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 24019, 236888, 768, 35627, 2226, 122333, 145453, 47926, 531, 1778, 236761, 107, 4754, 2765, 2863, 528, 1041, 28834, 3785, 3892, 3184, 236761, 107, 4573, 1299, 12502, 496, 9338, 528, 1041, 2228, 236764, 107, 11407, 1385, 564, 4355, 1041, 2668, 1374, 1520