INFO 09-15 16:10:58 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-0b882fbcb8f04227afd70a3bad268c87-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nLike feeble age, he reeleth from the day,\nSo should the lines of life that life repair,\nUnthrifty loveliness, why dost thou spend\nTill Nature, as she wrought thee, fell a-doting,\nIf thou couldst answer 'This fair child of mine\nAnd by addition me of thee defeated,\nTen times thyself were happier than thou art,\nAnd there reigns love and all love's loving parts,\nPoints on me graciously with fair aspect\nYou had a father: let your son say so.\nWhilst I, whom fortune of such triumph bars,\nLooking on darkness which the blind do see\n'Had my friend's Muse grown with this growing age,\nYou had a father: let your son say so.\nAn eye more bright than theirs, less false in rolling,\nBe not self-will'd, for thou art much too fair\nNor draw no lines there with thine antique pen;\nTo be death's conquest and make worms thine heir.\nThough yet, heaven knows, it is but as a tomb\nThis were to be new made when thou art old,\nIn our two loves there is but one respect,\nAnd they are rich and ransom all ill deeds.\nAs an unperfect actor on the stage\nI sigh the lack of many a thing I sought,\nTheirs for their style I'll read, his for his love.'\nMay make seem bare, in wanting words to show it,\nEven so my sun one early morn did shine\nWhich though it alter not love's sole effect,\nExceeded by the height of happier men.<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 17729, 105868, 3911, 236764, 668, 544, 7159, 594, 699, 506, 1719, 236764, 107, 4324, 1374, 506, 4463, 529, 1972, 600, 1972, 11790, 236764, 107, 2805, 594, 12544, 1363, 7278, 48636, 236764, 3217, 24873, 35627, 8559, 107, 112222, 15007, 23676