INFO 09-15 16:11:08 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-685b54159aca4f31a7941fe8901e6bc2-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nWhich to repair should be thy chief desire.\nBut if thou live, remember'd not to be,\nHow much more praise deserved thy beauty's use,\nIn our two loves there is but one respect,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nExceeded by the height of happier men.\nFor thou art so possess'd with murderous hate\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nAnd see the brave day sunk in hideous night;\nFor to thy sensual fault I bring in sense--\nMaking a couplement of proud compare,\nI summon up remembrance of things past,\nThe offender's sorrow lends but weak relief\nThat I in thy abundance am sufficed\nGilding the object whereupon it gazeth;\nFind no determination: then you were\nTill then not show my head where thou mayst prove me.\nWith all triumphant splendor on my brow;\nBearing thy heart, which I will keep so chary\nLeese but their show; their substance still lives sweet.\nMine be thy love and thy love's use their treasure.\nWhy lovest thou that which thou receivest not gladly,\nWith shifting change, as is false women's fashion;\nBut out, alack! he was but one hour mine;\nFind no determination: then you were\nThou mayst call thine when thou from youth convertest.\nAnd kept unused, the user so destroys it.\nThough yet, heaven knows, it is but as a tomb<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 24249, 531, 11790, 1374, 577, 21820, 9329, 12614, 236761, 107, 4573, 768, 35627, 3892, 236764, 5630, 236789, 236753, 711, 531, 577, 236764, 107, 3910, 1623, 919, 30450, 52026, 21820, 9899, 236789, 236751, 1161, 236764, 107, 902, 1023, 1156, 1817