INFO 09-15 16:11:46 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-855274fb82aa411c9768ca41cc2487bc-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nBut out, alack! he was but one hour mine;\nLet them say more than like of hearsay well;\nAh! but those tears are pearl which thy love sheds,\nAuthorizing thy trespass with compare,\nNature's bequest gives nothing but doth lend,\nBearing thy heart, which I will keep so chary\nFind no determination: then you were\nHim in thy course untainted do allow\nAnd stretched metre of an antique song:\nNor shall Death brag thou wander'st in his shade,\nThen how, when nature calls thee to be gone,\nThat due of many now is thine alone:\nAnd make the earth devour her own sweet brood;\nYet eyes this cunning want to grace their art;\nAnd every fair from fair sometime declines,\nLike feeble age, he reeleth from the day,\nSo is it not with me as with that Muse\nBe not self-will'd, for thou art much too fair\nExceeded by the height of happier men.\nWho all their parts of me to thee did give;\nThat use is not forbidden usury,\nOf his self-love, to stop posterity?\nOf his self-love, to stop posterity?\nAnd wear their brave state out of memory;\nWithout thy help by me be borne alone.\nO' let me, true in love, but truly write,\nOr to thyself at least kind-hearted prove:\nWhen every private widow well may keep\nThe lovely gaze where every eye doth dwell,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 4573, 855, 236764, 610, 697, 236888, 668, 691, 840, 886, 6468, 10701, 236793, 107, 6481, 1091, 1879, 919, 1082, 1133, 529, 114352, 1388, 236793, 107, 24019, 236888, 840, 1724, 24947, 659, 48361, 837, 21820, 2765, 87719, 236764, 107, 14953, 4266, 21820, 80922, 607, 10769, 236764, 107, 46797, 236789, 236751, 213797, 502