INFO 09-15 16:12:07 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-78fdc190556648e5919546bd6fc2e020-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nWhy didst thou promise such a beauteous day,\nWill play the tyrants to the very same\nWho heaven itself for ornament doth use\nWhich husbandry in honour might uphold\nMy body is the frame wherein 'tis held,\nWith all triumphant splendor on my brow;\nWhich happies those that pay the willing loan;\nWhen your sweet issue your sweet form should bear.\nWith what I most enjoy contented least;\nBut that thou none lovest is most evident;\nLet those whom Nature hath not made for store,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nFor thou art so possess'd with murderous hate\nFor thy sweet love remember'd such wealth brings\nMine eye hath play'd the painter and hath stell'd\nMine eyes have drawn thy shape, and thine for me\nStrikes each in each by mutual ordering,\nThe dear repose for limbs with travel tired;\nThough in our lives a separable spite,\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nBe scorn'd like old men of less truth than tongue,\nBut wherefore do not you a mightier way\nFor beauty's pattern to succeeding men.\nI sigh the lack of many a thing I sought,\nLo! thus, by day my limbs, by night my mind,\nAs a decrepit father takes delight\nAnd all the rest forgot for which he toil'd:\nThy merit hath my duty strongly knit,\nSo long as men can breathe or eyes can see,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 11355, 1602, 540, 35627, 14468, 1288, 496, 210820, 1328, 806, 1719, 236764, 107, 15600, 1441, 506, 50809, 1639, 531, 506, 1401, 1638, 107, 15938, 20808, 4850, 573, 20794, 139092, 1161, 107, 24249, 147305, 528, 20488, 2473, 83082, 107, 4754, 2742, 563, 506, 5528, 19139, 756, 55188, 4247,