INFO 09-15 16:12:17 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-05d5c57af468412c94693d74e96e30fe-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nFor through the painter must you see his skill,\nO' let me, true in love, but truly write,\nBut since she prick'd thee out for women's pleasure,\nTo give away yourself keeps yourself still,\nIn one of thine, from that which thou departest;\nSave that my soul's imaginary sight\nThen being ask'd where all thy beauty lies,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nFor precious friends hid in death's dateless night,\nNor lose possession of that fair thou owest;\nMay make seem bare, in wanting words to show it,\nUnless thou take that honour from thy name:\nPresents thy shadow to my sightless view,\nAh! if thou issueless shalt hap to die.\nFor then my thoughts, from far where I abide,\nAs truth and beauty shall together thrive,\nAnd many maiden gardens yet unset\nWhen I behold the violet past prime,\nBy oft predict that I in heaven find:\nIf from thyself to store thou wouldst convert;\nThat am debarr'd the benefit of rest?\nSo thou through windows of thine age shall see\nAnd though they be outstripp'd by every pen,\nThe perfect ceremony of love's rite,\nBy children's eyes her husband's shape in mind.\nDuty so great, which wit so poor as mine\nIf thou couldst answer 'This fair child of mine\nThy unused beauty must be tomb'd with thee,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 2542, 1343, 506, 42289, 1921, 611, 1460, 914, 12889, 236764, 107, 236806, 236789, 1531, 786, 236764, 1847, 528, 2765, 236764, 840, 9995, 4903, 236764, 107, 4573, 2338, 1304, 115426, 236789, 236753, 44543, 855, 573, 3607