INFO 09-15 16:12:27 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-a0d059bcb8eb43899fffb8833b886fa5-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nMusic to hear, why hear'st thou music sadly?\nAlthough our undivided loves are one:\nWhich erst from heat did canopy the herd,\nAnd all those friends which I thought buried.\nBut when from highmost pitch, with weary car,\nThat then I scorn to change my state with kings.\nThe region cloud hath mask'd him from me now.\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nStrikes each in each by mutual ordering,\nAh! but those tears are pearl which thy love sheds,\nUnthrifty loveliness, why dost thou spend\nShall I compare thee to a summer's day?\nThough in our lives a separable spite,\nDelights to peep, to gaze therein on thee;\nWhich, used, lives th' executor to be.\nOf public honour and proud titles boast,\nAs those gold candles fix'd in heaven's air:\nCan make you live yourself in eyes of men.\nLo! thus, by day my limbs, by night my mind,\nUnlook'd for joy in that I honour most.\nWhy lovest thou that which thou receivest not gladly,\nSave that my soul's imaginary sight\nWith April's first-born flowers, and all things rare\nResembling sire and child and happy mother\nAnd dumb presagers of my speaking breast,\nAnd stretched metre of an antique song:\nThy end is truth's and beauty's doom and date.\nAnd yet methinks I have astronomy,\nFor at a frown they in their glory die.<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 24068, 531, 6899, 236764, 3217, 6899, 236789, 540, 35627, 4252, 46149, 236881, 107, 13518, 1023, 161968, 18178, 659, 886, 236787, 107, 24249, 27461, 699, 5387, 1602, 56669, 506, 38340, 236764, 107, 3133, 784, 1724, 4690, 837, 564, 3305, 29051, 236761, 107, 4573, 1056, 699,