INFO 09-15 16:12:37 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-fba1dc854ef94d03b17632989a3673b9-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nAnd many maiden gardens yet unset\nAs I, not for myself, but for thee will;\nHung with the trophies of my lovers gone,\nNo longer yours than you yourself here live:\nThen look I death my days should expiate.\nVaunt in their youthful sap, at height decrease,\nAttending on his golden pilgrimage;\nLet those who are in favour with their stars\nDuty so great, which wit so poor as mine\nThy adverse party is thy advocate--\nWho for thyself art so unprovident.\nTo him that bears the strong offence's cross.\nWhat acceptable audit canst thou leave?\nThy beauty's form in table of my heart;\nRoses have thorns, and silver fountains mud;\nBut I forbid thee one most heinous crime:\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nMay make seem bare, in wanting words to show it,\nLook, what is best, that best I wish in thee:\nLike to the lark at break of day arising\nAnd all the rest forgot for which he toil'd:\nBut since he died and poets better prove,\nHung with the trophies of my lovers gone,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nFeatured like him, like him with friends possess'd,\nWith virtuous wish would bear your living flowers,\nBut day by night, and night by day, oppress'd?\nWhich I by lacking have supposed dead,\nThe sad account of fore-bemoaned moan,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 3133, 1551, 68602, 26318, 3819, 90520, 107, 2205, 564, 236764, 711, 573, 7564, 236764, 840, 573, 44543, 795, 236793, 107, 61625, 607, 506, 93529, 529, 1041, 31881, 8731, 236764, 107, 3771, 4890, 23149, 1082, 611, 5869, 1590, 3892, 236787, 107, 11407, 1385, 564, 4355, 1041, 2668, 1374, 1520, 17