INFO 09-15 16:12:37 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-bc2f2bd8b32e45219e62daaf10b1bbbf-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nWhereon the stars in secret influence comment;\n'Had my friend's Muse grown with this growing age,\nAnd wear their brave state out of memory;\nNor draw no lines there with thine antique pen;\nDevouring Time, blunt thou the lion's paws,\nSo I, for fear of trust, forget to say\nWho will believe my verse in time to come,\nI all alone beweep my outcast state\nSuch heavenly touches ne'er touch'd earthly faces.'\nA dearer birth than this his love had brought,\nSets you most rich in youth before my sight,\nTo the wide world and all her fading sweets;\nAnd being frank she lends to those are free.\nPoints on me graciously with fair aspect\nTill whatsoever star that guides my moving\nThy beauty's form in table of my heart;\nAnd barren rage of death's eternal cold?\nAs, thou being mine, mine is thy good report.\nThe age to come would say 'This poet lies:\nAs any mother's child, though not so bright\nWhose strength's abundance weakens his own heart.\nTo him that bears the strong offence's cross.\nThy beauty's form in table of my heart;\nThy unused beauty must be tomb'd with thee,\nBut not to tell of good or evil luck,\nWho will believe my verse in time to come,\nFor all that beauty that doth cover thee\nThy adverse party is thy advocate--\nThen can I drown an eye, unused to flow,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 10936, 498, 506, 8197, 528, 6789, 7630, 5739, 236793, 107, 236789, 55327, 1041, 4389, 236789, 236751, 41554, 12530, 607, 672, 6730, 3911, 236764, 107, 3133, 8785, 910, 36711, 1883, 855, 529, 6571, 236793, 107, 31777, 4988, 951, 4463, 993, 607, 162531, 34323, 4306, 236793, 107, 1