INFO 09-15 16:12:48 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-8fe971615f6d41dc81ec8af42df89a56-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nFor having traffic with thyself alone,\nThat heals the wound and cures not the disgrace:\nFeatured like him, like him with friends possess'd,\nTo be death's conquest and make worms thine heir.\nUnlook'd for joy in that I honour most.\nWith what I most enjoy contented least;\nDisdains the tillage of thy husbandry?\nThou dost beguile the world, unbless some mother.\nRough winds do shake the darling buds of May,\nWhereon the stars in secret influence comment;\nThat 'gainst thyself thou stick'st not to conspire.\nAnd puts apparel on my tatter'd loving,\nShall I compare thee to a summer's day?\nO, change thy thought, that I may change my mind!\nBeauty o'ersnow'd and bareness every where:\nMake war upon this bloody tyrant, Time?\nBorne on the bier with white and bristly beard,\nWith beauty's treasure, ere it be self-kill'd.\nAnd, constant stars, in them I read such art\nIs but the seemly raiment of my heart,\nAs a decrepit father takes delight\nLord of my love, to whom in vassalage\nWill play the tyrants to the very same\nIn one of thine, from that which thou departest;\nThen of thy beauty do I question make,\nMy body is the frame wherein 'tis held,\nNor thou with public kindness honour me,\nThen happy I, that love and am beloved\nIf ten of thine ten times refigured thee:<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 2542, 2963, 8827, 607, 208224, 883, 7057, 236764, 107, 6372, 153133, 506, 16753, 532, 110863, 711, 506, 87270, 236787, 107, 83917, 1133, 1515, 236764, 1133, 1515, 607, 4690, 12868, 236789, 236753, 236764, 107, 2021, 577, 4355, 236789, 236751, 69393, 532, 1386, 68468, 162531, 49967