INFO 09-15 16:12:58 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-389ead886c304e0687459a6f2d274c46-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nSo long as men can breathe or eyes can see,\nAnd stretched metre of an antique song:\nAnd loathsome canker lives in sweetest bud.\nAnd look upon myself and curse my fate,\nThat beauty still may live in thine or thee.\nBy children's eyes her husband's shape in mind.\nWhen every private widow well may keep\nSets you most rich in youth before my sight,\nWhich I new pay as if not paid before.\nFor all that beauty that doth cover thee\nMay make seem bare, in wanting words to show it,\nLooking on darkness which the blind do see\nAnd sable curls all silver'd o'er with white;\nWhich this, Time's pencil, or my pupil pen,\nYou had a father: let your son say so.\nNow see what good turns eyes for eyes have done:\nTo hear with eyes belongs to love's fine wit.\nNor can thy shame give physic to my grief;\nThen being ask'd where all thy beauty lies,\nI summon up remembrance of things past,\nThen can I grieve at grievances foregone,\nUnless thou take that honour from thy name:\nGilding the object whereupon it gazeth;\nWhy lovest thou that which thou receivest not gladly,\nThen, beauteous niggard, why dost thou abuse\nCalls back the lovely April of her prime:\nProving his beauty by succession thine!\nResembling sire and child and happy mother\nThen, were not summer's distillation left,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 4324, 1440, 618, 1758, 740, 38893, 653, 6114, 740, 1460, 236764, 107, 3133, 39349, 58194, 529, 614, 34323, 5410, 236787, 107, 3133, 1510, 651, 19256, 740, 5806, 6176, 528, 155753, 5207, 236761, 107, 3133, 1385, 3324, 7564, 532, 57391, 1041, 26334, 236764, 107, 6372, 9899, 2036, 