INFO 09-15 16:12:58 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-b8c262c1ea41470e9b4d31bf75a4fd5c-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nNow stand you on the top of happy hours,\nAnd in mine own love's strength seem to decay,\nFor all that beauty that doth cover thee\nThough in our lives a separable spite,\nAnd heavily from woe to woe tell o'er\nAnd in mine own love's strength seem to decay,\nI may not evermore acknowledge thee,\nAnd though they be outstripp'd by every pen,\nThen how, when nature calls thee to be gone,\nNor draw no lines there with thine antique pen;\nWithout this, folly, age and cold decay:\nIs from the book of honour razed quite,\nFor thee and for myself no quiet find.\nThe world will be thy widow and still weep\nFind no determination: then you were\nNor can I fortune to brief minutes tell,\nAs he takes from you, I engraft you new.\nOr else of thee this I prognosticate:\nPresume not on thy heart when mine is slain;\nThy unused beauty must be tomb'd with thee,\nIs but the seemly raiment of my heart,\nAuthorizing thy trespass with compare,\nThen look I death my days should expiate.\nSo great a sum of sums, yet canst not live?\nAnd each, though enemies to either's reign,\nWhere all the treasure of thy lusty days,\nBut thy eternal summer shall not fade\nHast thou, the master-mistress of my passion;<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 6445, 1975, 611, 580, 506, 1903, 529, 5293, 3885, 236764, 107, 3133, 528, 10701, 1852, 2765, 236789, 236751, 6332, 4483, 531, 17538, 236764, 107, 2542, 784, 600, 9899, 600, 139092, 2890, 44543, 107, 31382, 528, 1023, 6176, 496, 82155, 28719, 236764, 107, 3133, 18677, 69