INFO 09-15 16:12:58 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-2a06ce2003b64a578f8e01f9ea3b2630-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nShe carved thee for her seal, and meant thereby\nThose hours, that with gentle work did frame\nRough winds do shake the darling buds of May,\nThen of thy beauty do I question make,\nStrikes each in each by mutual ordering,\nFor whether beauty, birth, or wealth, or wit,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nNot from the stars do I my judgment pluck;\nNo longer yours than you yourself here live:\nPointing to each his thunder, rain and wind,\nLike to the lark at break of day arising\nO'ercharged with burden of mine own love's might.\nThen what could death do, if thou shouldst depart,\nServing with looks his sacred majesty;\nFor then my thoughts, from far where I abide,\nNo longer yours than you yourself here live:\nIn our two loves there is but one respect,\nAnd all in war with Time for love of you,\nAnd look upon myself and curse my fate,\nYet, do thy worst, old Time: despite thy wrong,\nOr ten times happier, be it ten for one;\nWhen lofty trees I see barren of leaves\nDelights to peep, to gaze therein on thee;\nAnd heavily from woe to woe tell o'er\nThat thou among the wastes of time must go,\nFind no determination: then you were\nTo change your day of youth to sullied night;\nWhen that churl Death my bones with dust shall cover,\nHow much more praise deserved thy beauty's use,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 5778, 39043, 44543, 573, 1116, 18505, 236764, 532, 9655, 17534, 107, 28587, 3885, 236764, 600, 607, 14617, 981, 1602, 5528, 107, 122700, 29146, 776, 31716, 506, 96018, 43814, 529, 3353, 236764, 107, 11407, 529, 21820, 9899, 776, 564, 2934, 1386, 23676