INFO 09-15 16:12:58 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-032534ce729c4d8ebbfefdc1ec3c4b29-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nO, carve not with thy hours my love's fair brow,\n'Tis not enough that through the cloud thou break,\nWhich in thy breast doth live, as thine in me:\nOf public honour and proud titles boast,\nMake sweet some vial; treasure thou some place\nProfitless usurer, why dost thou use\nMake war upon this bloody tyrant, Time?\nFor thee and for myself no quiet find.\nAnd trouble deal heaven with my bootless cries\nAnd summer's green all girded up in sheaves\nFor thy sweet love remember'd such wealth brings\nThe age to come would say 'This poet lies:\nMuch liker than your painted counterfeit:\nLeese but their show; their substance still lives sweet.\nWhich husbandry in honour might uphold\nThat use is not forbidden usury,\nTake all my comfort of thy worth and truth.\nShall sum my count and make my old excuse,'\nAnd dost him grace when clouds do blot the heaven:\nDuty so great, which wit so poor as mine\nTheir images I loved I view in thee,\nThou art more lovely and more temperate:\nWhen I behold the violet past prime,\nDo in consent shake hands to torture me;\nShall I compare thee to a summer's day?\nAnd weep afresh love's long since cancell'd woe,\nAnd in fresh numbers number all your graces,\nThen of thy beauty do I question make,\nWhich happies those that pay the willing loan;<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 236806, 236764, 107478, 711, 607, 21820, 3885, 1041, 2765, 236789, 236751, 5888, 69135, 236764, 107, 236789, 112728, 711, 3487, 600, 1343, 506, 6425, 35627, 2541, 236764, 107, 24249, 528, 21820, 16489, 139092, 3892, 236764, 618, 162531, 528, 786, 236787, 107, 4088, 1237, 20488, 