INFO 09-15 16:13:09 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-0a02e12755d44b8283cbbeef6e19bf13-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nDuty so great, which wit so poor as mine\nAnd in fresh numbers number all your graces,\nThen may I dare to boast how I do love thee;\nAnd every fair with his fair doth rehearse\nAs interest of the dead, which now appear\nAnd in themselves their pride lies buried,\nAnd shalt by fortune once more re-survey\nAnd in themselves their pride lies buried,\nFor precious friends hid in death's dateless night,\nBut wherefore do not you a mightier way\nShall I compare thee to a summer's day?\nAs truth and beauty shall together thrive,\nWhich I new pay as if not paid before.\nI sigh the lack of many a thing I sought,\nWith shifting change, as is false women's fashion;\nIs but the seemly raiment of my heart,\nNor can I fortune to brief minutes tell,\nO, that you were yourself! but, love, you are\nAnd that unfair which fairly doth excel:\nShall hate be fairer lodged than gentle love?\nThen what could death do, if thou shouldst depart,\nMake sweet some vial; treasure thou some place\nAnd sable curls all silver'd o'er with white;\nThe region cloud hath mask'd him from me now.\nWhose strength's abundance weakens his own heart.\nAnd barren rage of death's eternal cold?\nIn our two loves there is but one respect,\nTo that sweet thief which sourly robs from me.\nBeauty's effect with beauty were bereft,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 116195, 834, 1822, 236764, 837, 32950, 834, 6934, 618, 10701, 107, 3133, 528, 5756, 4945, 1548, 784, 822, 185518, 236764, 107, 11407, 1149, 564, 30253, 531, 70447, 1217, 564, 776, 2765, 44543, 236793, 107, 3133, 1418, 5888, 607, 914, 5888, 139092, 236588, 107, 2205