INFO 09-15 16:13:56 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-cfb0e5f7ddc54e5ea646aa093514195c-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nBut flowers distill'd though they with winter meet,\nMuch steals men's eyes and women's souls amazeth.\nSo long as men can breathe or eyes can see,\nAs I, not for myself, but for thee will;\nThe age to come would say 'This poet lies:\nAnd keep my drooping eyelids open wide,\nMine be thy love and thy love's use their treasure.\nLet those who are in favour with their stars\n'Had my friend's Muse grown with this growing age,\nNature's bequest gives nothing but doth lend,\nReserve them for my love, not for their rhyme,\nAnd kept unused, the user so destroys it.\nBut do not so; I love thee in such sort\nBut were some child of yours alive that time,\nAnd many maiden gardens yet unset\nAs a decrepit father takes delight\nO' let me, true in love, but truly write,\nHow much more praise deserved thy beauty's use,\nWhy didst thou promise such a beauteous day,\nAnd that fresh blood which youngly thou bestowest\nTo change your day of youth to sullied night;\nThat use is not forbidden usury,\nAnd by a part of all thy glory live.\nAre windows to my breast, where-through the sun\nFor no man well of such a salve can speak\nTo hear with eyes belongs to love's fine wit.\nTheirs for their style I'll read, his for his love.'\nAnon permit the basest clouds to ride\nWhich though it alter not love's sole effect,<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 4573, 7983, 102083, 236789, 236753, 3635, 901, 607, 7208, 2874, 236764, 107, 46003, 88541, 1758, 236789, 236751, 6114, 532, 3607, 236789, 236751, 39690, 6660, 1064, 236761, 107, 4324, 1440, 618, 1758, 740, 38893, 653, 6114, 740, 1460, 236764, 107, 2205, 564,