 10%|█         | 100/1000 [00:12<01:17, 11.68it/s]INFO 09-15 16:14:08 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-e589e76b88454415a90c3049661cd3b9-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nSave breed, to brave him when he takes thee hence.\nSo long as men can breathe or eyes can see,\nLooking on darkness which the blind do see\nAnd trouble deal heaven with my bootless cries\nIf all were minded so, the times should cease\nThen look I death my days should expiate.\nWith ugly rack on his celestial face,\nThou art thy mother's glass, and she in thee\nThou art the grave where buried love doth live,\nTill then not show my head where thou mayst prove me.\nThou art the grave where buried love doth live,\nYet him for this my love no whit disdaineth;\nHow far I toil, still farther off from thee.\nAfter a thousand victories once foil'd,\nSo great a sum of sums, yet canst not live?\nSo long as youth and thou are of one date;\nWill be a tatter'd weed, of small worth held:\nThough yet, heaven knows, it is but as a tomb\nUpon thyself thy beauty's legacy?\nO'ercharged with burden of mine own love's might.\nThy youth's proud livery, so gazed on now,\nBut day by night, and night by day, oppress'd?\nAfter a thousand victories once foil'd,\nUpon thyself thy beauty's legacy?\nNor it nor no remembrance what it was:\nYet in these thoughts myself almost despising,\nHow far I toil, still farther off from thee.\nNor can thy shame give physic to my grief;\nYou had a father: let your son say so.<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 14000, 22868, 236764, 531, 36711, 1515, 1056, 668, 4716, 44543, 11632, 236761, 107, 4324, 1440, 618, 1758, 740, 38893, 653, 6114, 740, 1460, 236764, 107, 30988, 580, 29151, 837, 506, 18261, 776, 1460, 107, 3133, 13