INFO 09-15 16:14:08 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-762b093613ad4b41b9245bf9dde83619-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nSave breed, to brave him when he takes thee hence.\nAnd thou, all they, hast all the all of me.\nWhen I perceive that men as plants increase,\nFor never-resting time leads summer on\nMay make seem bare, in wanting words to show it,\nThe eyes, 'fore duteous, now converted are\nThough thou repent, yet I have still the loss:\nLo! thus, by day my limbs, by night my mind,\nDo in consent shake hands to torture me;\nBorne on the bier with white and bristly beard,\nIn our two loves there is but one respect,\nWith means more blessed than my barren rhyme?\nMake thee another self, for love of me,\nWhilst I, whom fortune of such triumph bars,\nBut things removed that hidden in thee lie!\nThy adverse party is thy advocate--\nAnd many maiden gardens yet unset\nAnd each, though enemies to either's reign,\nAnd being frank she lends to those are free.\nAll men make faults, and even I in this,\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nSo is it not with me as with that Muse\nThou shouldst print more, not let that copy die.\nVaunt in their youthful sap, at height decrease,\nIf I could write the beauty of your eyes\nMake glad and sorry seasons as thou fleets,\nBut if the while I think on thee, dear friend,\nBut thy eternal summer shall not fade\nNor draw no lines there with thine antique pen;<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 14000, 22868, 236764, 531, 36711, 1515, 1056, 668, 4716, 44543, 11632, 236761, 107, 3133, 35627, 236764, 784, 901, 236764, 23823, 784, 506, 784, 529, 786, 236761, 107, 4420, 564, 48672, 600, 1758, 618, 6485, 3553, 236764, 107, 2542, 2752, 236772, 197012, 990, 9025, 53