INFO 09-15 16:14:08 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-06c332d7788f480ea9d2782194505093-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nAs fast as thou shalt wane, so fast thou growest\nThe painful warrior famoused for fight,\nThat am debarr'd the benefit of rest?\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nFor through the painter must you see his skill,\nMake glad and sorry seasons as thou fleets,\nFor at a frown they in their glory die.\nAnd look upon myself and curse my fate,\nWhen forty winters shall beseige thy brow,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nAttending on his golden pilgrimage;\nPointing to each his thunder, rain and wind,\nMake glad and sorry seasons as thou fleets,\nThat heaven's air in this huge rondure hems.\nYet in these thoughts myself almost despising,\nAs he takes from you, I engraft you new.\nExcusing thy sins more than thy sins are;\nThat then I scorn to change my state with kings.\nI may not evermore acknowledge thee,\nThat due of many now is thine alone:\nBut day by night, and night by day, oppress'd?\nThou art more lovely and more temperate:\nThat I in thy abundance am sufficed\nAnd, constant stars, in them I read such art\nLo! in the orient when the gracious light\nStealing unseen to west with this disgrace:\nThou art more lovely and more temperate:\nTheirs for their style I'll read, his for his love.'\nAnd summer's lease hath all too short a date:<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 2205, 4592, 618, 35627, 145453, 515, 1629, 236764, 834, 4592, 35627, 2171, 598, 107, 818, 27668, 45850, 9639, 524, 573, 6093, 236764, 107, 6372, 1006, 569, 2230, 236750, 236789, 236753, 506, 7458, 529, 1884, 236881, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 2542, 1343, 506, 4