INFO 09-15 16:14:08 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-508ffb19e6bd44dd8a160412ab6e5778-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWeary with toil, I haste me to my bed,\nAnd all those friends which I thought buried.\nThy adverse party is thy advocate--\nThat due of many now is thine alone:\nAll losses are restored and sorrows end.\nWithout thy help by me be borne alone.\nWhen I perceive that men as plants increase,\nShifts but his place, for still the world enjoys it;\nWill play the tyrants to the very same\nOr ten times happier, be it ten for one;\nLo! in the orient when the gracious light\nIf from thyself to store thou wouldst convert;\nMy glass shall not persuade me I am old,\nThy unused beauty must be tomb'd with thee,\nAnd trouble deal heaven with my bootless cries\nAll losses are restored and sorrows end.\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nMake war upon this bloody tyrant, Time?\nMake thee another self, for love of me,\nThough in our lives a separable spite,\nWith what I most enjoy contented least;\nYet, do thy worst, old Time: despite thy wrong,\nWho heaven itself for ornament doth use\nAnd being frank she lends to those are free.\nAnd yet methinks I have astronomy,\nThen can I drown an eye, unused to flow,\nOr who is he so fond will be the tomb\nAnd barren rage of death's eternal cold?<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 103664, 236762, 607, 141001, 236764, 564, 104337, 786, 531, 1041, 4086, 236764, 107, 3133, 784, 1724, 4690, 837, 564, 3305, 29051, 236761, 107, 195297, 23779, 4598, 563, 21820, 32371, 726, 107, 6372, 2779, 529, 1551, 1492, 563, 162531, 7057, 236787, 107, 3243, 14672, 6