INFO 09-15 16:14:08 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-be5249d31bc44d39bc4dc89dd8f60545-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nSo great a sum of sums, yet canst not live?\nTo march in ranks of better equipage:\nCompare them with the bettering of the time,\nIf all were minded so, the times should cease\nAs any mother's child, though not so bright\nLeese but their show; their substance still lives sweet.\nAnd each, though enemies to either's reign,\nAnd stretched metre of an antique song:\nThat this huge stage presenteth nought but shows\nMyself corrupting, salving thy amiss,\nThou art the grave where buried love doth live,\nAnd shalt by fortune once more re-survey\nWhich I new pay as if not paid before.\nLo! thus, by day my limbs, by night my mind,\nTo dry the rain on my storm-beaten face,\nAnd die as fast as they see others grow;\nNo more be grieved at that which thou hast done:\nAnd many maiden gardens yet unset\nBut day doth daily draw my sorrows longer\nAnd barren rage of death's eternal cold?\nAnd every fair from fair sometime declines,\nGrant, if thou wilt, thou art beloved of many,\nFor never-resting time leads summer on\nAnd die as fast as they see others grow;\nAnd see thy blood warm when thou feel'st it cold.\nBorne on the bier with white and bristly beard,\nNo longer yours than you yourself here live:\nBut if thou live, remember'd not to be,\nThen look I death my days should expiate.<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 4324, 1822, 496, 2324, 529, 31945, 236764, 3819, 740, 540, 711, 3892, 236881, 107, 2021, 14868, 528, 26867, 529, 2480, 4653, 676, 236787, 107, 44438, 1091, 607, 506, 2480, 522, 529, 506, 990, 236764, 107, 2859, 784, 964, 90971, 834, 236764, 506, 2782, 1374, 41013, 107, 2205, 10