INFO 09-15 16:14:08 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-c8385a0cbc7e439bb77819c7d66579cb-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nSo should that beauty which you hold in lease\nWhere wasteful Time debateth with Decay,\nBy unions married, do offend thine ear,\nAn eye more bright than theirs, less false in rolling,\nCompare them with the bettering of the time,\nMore than that tongue that more hath more express'd.\nO, therefore, love, be of thyself so wary\nMake war upon this bloody tyrant, Time?\nWhen forty winters shall beseige thy brow,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nTill Nature, as she wrought thee, fell a-doting,\nIs from the book of honour razed quite,\nUnlook'd for joy in that I honour most.\nMy glass shall not persuade me I am old,\nThe age to come would say 'This poet lies:\nHath dear religious love stol'n from mine eye\nA dearer birth than this his love had brought,\nFrom sullen earth, sings hymns at heaven's gate;\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nThen look I death my days should expiate.\nBut day doth daily draw my sorrows longer\nLook, whom she best endow'd she gave the more;\nBut that thou none lovest is most evident;\nThat heaven's air in this huge rondure hems.\nAnd heavily from woe to woe tell o'er\nA woman's gentle heart, but not acquainted\nIf it were fill'd with your most high deserts?\nWith all triumphant splendor on my brow;\nWho all their parts of me to thee did give;<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 4324, 1374, 600, 9899, 837, 611, 2768, 528, 20850, 107, 10936, 128208, 7578, 233416, 1064, 607, 162935, 236764, 107, 2292, 31592, 11578, 236764, 776, 125227, 162531, 10222, 236764, 107, 2267, 7068, 919, 7804, 1082, 61877, 236764, 2344, 2416, 528, 19519, 236764, 