INFO 09-15 16:14:08 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-50d6bbe2942d495f9e6e52d5dfc00cb5-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nThou gavest me thine, not to give back again.\nThen may I dare to boast how I do love thee;\nClouds and eclipses stain both moon and sun,\nThe dear repose for limbs with travel tired;\nFor through the painter must you see his skill,\nWhich bounteous gift thou shouldst in bounty cherish:\nO, then vouchsafe me but this loving thought:\nHath dear religious love stol'n from mine eye\nFeatured like him, like him with friends possess'd,\nThat am debarr'd the benefit of rest?\nThat am debarr'd the benefit of rest?\nAnd weep afresh love's long since cancell'd woe,\nAs those gold candles fix'd in heaven's air:\nShall hate be fairer lodged than gentle love?\nHarsh featureless and rude, barrenly perish:\nSo shall those blots that do with me remain\nLifts up his burning head, each under eye\nShall I compare thee to a summer's day?\nTo say, within thine own deep-sunken eyes,\nWith sun and moon, with earth and sea's rich gems,\nDevouring Time, blunt thou the lion's paws,\nHerein lives wisdom, beauty and increase:\nWill be a tatter'd weed, of small worth held:\nAnd see the brave day sunk in hideous night;\nAnd then believe me, my love is as fair\nWith what I most enjoy contented least;\nWhen forty winters shall beseige thy brow,\nThe lovely gaze where every eye doth dwell,\nShall I compare thee to a summer's day?<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 178651, 106020, 598, 786, 162531, 236764, 711, 531, 2583, 1063, 1570, 236761, 107, 11407, 1149, 564, 30253, 531, 70447, 1217, 564, 776, 2765, 44543, 236793, 107, 102500, 532, 103516, 507, 15769, 1800, 16254, 532, 3768, 236764, 107, 818, 23348, 1051