INFO 09-15 16:14:31 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-78772f43394641279664a66fbc9eb343-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nSo long lives this and this gives life to thee.\nFrom his low tract and look another way:\nAnd then believe me, my love is as fair\nDo in consent shake hands to torture me;\nBut not to tell of good or evil luck,\nThen can I grieve at grievances foregone,\nIf from thyself to store thou wouldst convert;\nLet those whom Nature hath not made for store,\nResembling sire and child and happy mother\nAnd stretched metre of an antique song:\nOr some fierce thing replete with too much rage,\nWhere all the treasure of thy lusty days,\nProfitless usurer, why dost thou use\nTo witness duty, not to show my wit:\nSap cheque'd with frost and lusty leaves quite gone,\nSo should that beauty which you hold in lease\nBut then begins a journey in my head,\nSince sweets and beauties do themselves forsake\nAnd die as fast as they see others grow;\nDesiring this man's art and that man's scope,\nTill Nature, as she wrought thee, fell a-doting,\nAs tender nurse her babe from faring ill.\nAuthorizing thy trespass with compare,\nRoses have thorns, and silver fountains mud;\nOr say with princes if it shall go well,\nI tell the day, to please them thou art bright\nWhen, in disgrace with fortune and men's eyes,\nBut when from highmost pitch, with weary car,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 4324, 1440, 6176, 672, 532, 672, 5021, 1972, 531, 44543, 236761, 107, 4663, 914, 2708, 16359, 532, 1385, 2264, 1595, 236787, 107, 3133, 1299, 4646, 786, 236764, 1041, 2765, 563, 618, 5888, 107, 6294, 528, 13782, 31716, 4916, 531, 55313, 786, 236793, 107, 4573, 711, 531, 3442, 529,