INFO 09-15 16:14:31 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-e2234aa5ee0845358554f9beeae2b5d1-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nHath dear religious love stol'n from mine eye\nLook, whom she best endow'd she gave the more;\nThy adverse party is thy advocate--\nWhich in thy breast doth live, as thine in me:\nThat I in thy abundance am sufficed\nAnd your true rights be term'd a poet's rage\nA man in hue, all 'hues' in his controlling,\nTill whatsoever star that guides my moving\nBut day by night, and night by day, oppress'd?\nBy adding one thing to my purpose nothing.\nLet them say more than like of hearsay well;\nFor whether beauty, birth, or wealth, or wit,\nAs those gold candles fix'd in heaven's air:\nTo him that bears the strong offence's cross.\nAnd nothing 'gainst Time's scythe can make defence\nWhen, in disgrace with fortune and men's eyes,\nThou gavest me thine, not to give back again.\nAnd fortify yourself in your decay\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nSuns of the world may stain when heaven's sun staineth.\nPluck the keen teeth from the fierce tiger's jaws,\nKissing with golden face the meadows green,\nAnd all those friends which I thought buried.\nHarsh featureless and rude, barrenly perish:\nSo I, for fear of trust, forget to say\nIf thou survive my well-contented day,\nWhere I may not remove nor be removed.\nThat due of many now is thine alone:\nAnd your true rights be term'd a poet's rage<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 236814, 651, 23348, 12352, 2765, 64569, 236789, 236749, 699, 10701, 7068, 107, 13908, 236764, 8761, 1304, 1791, 142798, 236789, 236753, 1304, 5877, 506, 919, 236793, 107, 195297, 23779, 4598, 563, 21820, 32371, 726, 107, 24249, 528, 21820, 16489, 139092, 3892, 2