INFO 09-15 16:14:31 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-6a802d40d9bc44c992965fc9a34e9510-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nTo be death's conquest and make worms thine heir.\nNo more be grieved at that which thou hast done:\nBy adding one thing to my purpose nothing.\nAnd fortify yourself in your decay\nWhereon the stars in secret influence comment;\nHerein lives wisdom, beauty and increase:\nThen how, when nature calls thee to be gone,\nTen times thyself were happier than thou art,\nBut things removed that hidden in thee lie!\nWho heaven itself for ornament doth use\nMy love shall in my verse ever live young.\nBe not self-will'd, for thou art much too fair\nBut since he died and poets better prove,\nThy adverse party is thy advocate--\nThey draw but what they see, know not the heart.\nIf the true concord of well-tuned sounds,\nUnlook'd for joy in that I honour most.\nI make my love engrafted to this store:\nMy body is the frame wherein 'tis held,\nWhose strength's abundance weakens his own heart.\nA woman's face with Nature's own hand painted\nNot from the stars do I my judgment pluck;\nTake all my comfort of thy worth and truth.\nTo that sweet thief which sourly robs from me.\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nAnd your true rights be term'd a poet's rage\nWho all in one, one pleasing note do sing:\nBut then begins a journey in my head,\nIn thee thy summer, ere thou be distill'd:<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 2021, 577, 4355, 236789, 236751, 69393, 532, 1386, 68468, 162531, 49967, 236761, 107, 3771, 919, 577, 66031, 1872, 657, 600, 837, 35627, 23823, 3028, 236787, 107, 2292, 8009, 886, 3210, 531, 1041, 5708, 5017, 236761, 107, 3133, 7845, 1891, 5869, 528, 822, 17538, 107, 10936,