INFO 09-15 16:14:32 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-392e6b97aee64830bd7cb4c1308baa67-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nThou art the grave where buried love doth live,\nThen how, when nature calls thee to be gone,\nO'ercharged with burden of mine own love's might.\nLooking on darkness which the blind do see\nA liquid prisoner pent in walls of glass,\nAnd your sweet semblance to some other give.\nAnd then believe me, my love is as fair\nThen of thy beauty do I question make,\nBut I forbid thee one most heinous crime:\nO, therefore, love, be of thyself so wary\nAnd all those friends which I thought buried.\nBut since she prick'd thee out for women's pleasure,\nWho plead for love and look for recompense\nBy oft predict that I in heaven find:\nA woman's gentle heart, but not acquainted\nTo dry the rain on my storm-beaten face,\nKissing with golden face the meadows green,\nDuty so great, which wit so poor as mine\nIn our two loves there is but one respect,\nThen may I dare to boast how I do love thee;\nYou should live twice; in it and in my rhyme.\nStealing unseen to west with this disgrace:\nAnd perspective it is the painter's art.\nAnd by addition me of thee defeated,\nThe world will be thy widow and still weep\nBy children's eyes her husband's shape in mind.\nAnd night doth nightly make grief's strength seem stronger.\nBut not to tell of good or evil luck,\nLord of my love, to whom in vassalage<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 178651, 1610, 506, 23674, 1298, 29051, 2765, 139092, 3892, 236764, 107, 11407, 1217, 236764, 1056, 4135, 9139, 44543, 531, 577, 8731, 236764, 107, 236806, 236789, 497, 52989, 607, 18080, 529, 10701, 1852, 2765, 236789, 236751, 2473, 236761, 107, 30988, 580, 29151, 837, 50