INFO 09-15 16:14:32 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-a6cfce8221b9446cb1b81a54e4c560f3-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nAnd having climb'd the steep-up heavenly hill,\nDevouring Time, blunt thou the lion's paws,\nReserve them for my love, not for their rhyme,\nSo thou through windows of thine age shall see\nWhere I may not remove nor be removed.\nFrom his low tract and look another way:\nWhen I consider every thing that grows\nLet me confess that we two must be twain,\nYet him for this my love no whit disdaineth;\nAnd heavily from woe to woe tell o'er\nHim in thy course untainted do allow\nWhich I new pay as if not paid before.\nRoses have thorns, and silver fountains mud;\nAnd though they be outstripp'd by every pen,\nFor then my thoughts, from far where I abide,\nAnd threescore year would make the world away.\nYet doth it steal sweet hours from love's delight.\nMaking a couplement of proud compare,\nThat thou among the wastes of time must go,\nNow stand you on the top of happy hours,\nBut since he died and poets better prove,\nAs a decrepit father takes delight\nDespite of wrinkles this thy golden time.\nTo the wide world and all her fading sweets;\nEven so my sun one early morn did shine\nCan make you live yourself in eyes of men.\nEven so my sun one early morn did shine\nSap cheque'd with frost and lusty leaves quite gone,\nWho heaven itself for ornament doth use<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 3133, 2963, 17085, 236789, 236753, 506, 25465, 236772, 1048, 67110, 17971, 236764, 107, 11062, 114833, 7578, 236764, 63696, 35627, 506, 32329, 236789, 236751, 114386, 236764, 107, 133422, 1091, 573, 1041, 2765, 236764, 711, 573, 910, 117370, 236764, 107, 4324, 35627, 1343, 11665, 529, 162531, 3911