INFO 09-15 16:14:43 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-013f1cbbc4f14a57bb800c7a3550c47d-0: prompt: "<bos><start_of_turn>user\nPick as many lines as you can from these poem lines:\nFROM fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contracted to thine own bright eyes,\nFeed'st thy light'st flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\nThen can I drown an eye, unused to flow,\nBut when in thee time's furrows I behold,\nI all alone beweep my outcast state\nShall hate be fairer lodged than gentle love?\nMake glad and sorry seasons as thou fleets,\nBut then begins a journey in my head,\nAnd yet methinks I have astronomy,\nFor through the painter must you see his skill,\nWhen I do count the clock that tells the time,\nFor thy sweet love remember'd such wealth brings\nTen times thyself were happier than thou art,\nNeither in inward worth nor outward fair,\nBorne on the bier with white and bristly beard,\nAnd burn the long-lived phoenix in her blood;\nI tell the day, to please them thou art bright\nPluck the keen teeth from the fierce tiger's jaws,\nHow much more praise deserved thy beauty's use,\nAs, thou being mine, mine is thy good report.\nTo be death's conquest and make worms thine heir.\nLest my bewailed guilt should do thee shame,\nNo longer yours than you yourself here live:\nWhen lofty trees I see barren of leaves\nThen happy I, that love and am beloved\nFor at a frown they in their glory die.\nHarsh featureless and rude, barrenly perish:\nThen happy I, that love and am beloved\nTo show me worthy of thy sweet respect:\nHaply I think on thee, and then my state,\nTo him that bears the strong offence's cross.<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=150, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2, 105, 2364, 107, 42407, 618, 1551, 4463, 618, 611, 740, 699, 1239, 27355, 4463, 236787, 107, 28337, 12221, 540, 28682, 692, 12614, 3553, 236764, 107, 6372, 17534, 9899, 236789, 236751, 11076, 2473, 2752, 1778, 236764, 107, 4573, 618, 506, 3382, 721, 1374, 684, 990, 20401, 781, 236764, 107, 15989, 21870, 49967, 2473, 10591, 914, 6571, 236787, 107, 4573, 35627, 236764, 45987, 531, 162531, 1852, 7804, 6114, 236764, 107, 28923, 236789, 540, 21820, 2214, 236789, 540, 27400, 607, 1265, 236772, 189395, 7611, 236764, 107, 41950, 496, 93263, 1298, 26444, 12828, 236764, 107, 1214, 986, 883, 21820, 95521, 236764, 531, 21820, 9380, 1265, 2311, 34381, 236761, 107, 178651, 600, 1610, 1492, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 5756, 20794, 107, 3133, 1186, 81319, 531, 506, 11557, 66632, 6247, 236764, 107, 43794, 162531, 1852, 5207, 5717, 15163, 21820, 3004, 107, 3133, 236764, 21870, 677, 2451, 236764, 17216, 598, 8321, 528, 116063, 23485, 236761, 107, 236791, 665, 506, 1902, 236764, 653, 1663, 672, 2112, 1654, 577, 236764, 107, 2021, 9039, 506, 1902, 236789, 236751, 2779, 236764, 684, 506, 23674, 532, 44543, 236761, 107, 11407, 740, 564, 119491, 614, 7068, 236764, 50781, 531, 2727, 236764, 107, 4573, 1056, 528, 44543, 990, 236789, 236751, 13969, 4290, 564, 67028, 236764, 107, 236777, 784, 7057, 226362, 838, 1041, 236326, 1883, 107, 172702, 17554, 577, 173410, 81060, 1082, 14617, 2765, 